{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584212-running-a-one-shot-what-elements-should-i-emphasize-to-create-the-d-td-feel","id":584212,"title":"Running a one-shot - what elements should I emphasize to create the D:tD feel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-08T22:27:59-07:00","id":584212,"title":"Running a one-shot - what elements should I emphasize to create the D:tD feel?","content":"As the title says. Last week I got my copy of Demon: the Descent and - dear God - I must run this game <i>right now</i>. But that'll have to wait until this coming Tuesday.<br /> <br /> I wrote up a review of the game in Korean and people were interested. But I was so eager that I didn't really think through what the one-shot would be like. As in, what elements should I emphasize in the session? Covers? Creative usage of Embeds and Exploits? Pacts? Demonic inter-factional dealings? I'm at a loss since there are so many cool things in the game and I'm afraid I can't fit everything within a 4-hour long one-shot. D:<br /> <br /> The idea I'm having is... the PCs are operating in Seoul as free agents, but also in frequent contact with a Tempter-friendly Temporal Agency known as In Vino Veritas (whose front is obviously a bar). IVV lets the PCs in on the news that one of the city's major Facilities is expanding itself. And, well, they would like to offer more information but, as always, shit happens and the meeting is violently adjourned by mortal hunters sent by unknown parties. So it's up to the PCs to discover the missing information themselves. Infiltrating associated organizations, snooping around Infrastructure, spying on the G-M's agents and so on.<br /> <br /> In the end, it is revealed that the God-Machine is idly curious about the effect of a major city being destroyed from the face of Earth, so an occult weapon will be used to devastate Seoul - and the Facility was expanding to create a replacement Seoul, so the God-Machine can reset everything if the results aren't to its liking. The climactic scene would take inside the subterranean city-sized bunker, all with people in glass tubes and dimensionally folded skyscrapers. If the PCs themselves don't destroy the replacement, the previously unknown parties who disrupted IVV and the PCs' contact will - because they are a rival terrorist Agency, bent on destroying anything related to the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> From there on... I'll leave it to the PCs. I'd like to throw in a high-rank angel if the players want to fight something. I will also have to prepare a different challenge, too.<br /> <br /> Right now, I think this might be slightly more than what I can do with a 4/5-hour one-shot, so I'll have to trim down. But also, I need to add stuff that makes Demon a truly unique game.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions on how? D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3365-szp","name":"szp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3365_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T23:21:40-07:00","id":584286,"title":"","content":"I think the fundamental thing for a one shot (having run quite a few myself) is that you give the players a single, achievable goal from the outset. From what you've suggested up there, unless you want all the plot as stakes and window dressing, I feel like it'll be too much to accomplish. I could see that happening over maybe a set of 3-4 sessions of that length. Of course, the obvious thing of assume that the PCs are well established and know who they are, who their allies are and what their relationships are. The Goals system for NWOD characters is good, just make them all short term goals for the session. Earning beats can be substituted for earning Aether or Willpower for a one-shot game without breaking anything, too.<br /> <br /> One of my best experiences running (and from the players, playing) one shots was a Changeling one-shot that I ran at a convention a few years back. The PCs were a group of Loyalists who were staging a heist of a Freehold. There was a bit of fighting, a bit of sneaking around, a bit of talking/socialising, but they already had the &quot;key points&quot; so the game happened. Realistically, the entire game was about three Scenes, to use the Storyteller time parlance.<br /> <br /> You're not going to be able to give the full flavour of the game in one session, so pick which parts you want to show off. Do you want to show off the rebel/insurgent angle? Focus on the infrastructure. Do you want to focus on the cold war espionage? Focus on the Agency area. Want to focus on the body horror and weird science? Focus on making deals with Humans and competing with Angels.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend keeping the supernatural abilities simple if they don't have any system experience. Simplified character sheets/cheat sheets with just the key powers they'd want to use for their character. It's probably okay to template the Demonic forms too or even give them all the same basic form. The four embeds/exploits and maybe a form power or two should be enough to handle everything in a single session.<br /> <br /> Basically, pick one key thing to focus on and run with it - One-shots are too short to get into a breadth of subject and it needs to be tightly focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 07-09-2015, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T19:01:22-07:00","id":588704,"title":"","content":"I'm also planning on doing a DtD one-shot, but I'd decided to run a structure of: one procedural scene, one social scene, and one combat scene. <br /> <br /> I thought about including an Aether gathering scene, in the way that I might start a vampire one-shot off with a hunting sequence to set the mood. However, I'm not sure what a typical aether gathering looks like. Is it usually an infrastructure heist? Or looking for signs of angelic activity and scouring the area for dross? Or something else?<br /> <br /> Alternately, aether gathering might involve abusing a rule loophole of having one demon assume demon form, then repeatedly transferring all of its aether away and generating more by rolling primum at zero aether. I don't think I want to encourage that in the one-shot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T19:11:51-07:00","id":588722,"title":"","content":"Gathering Aether can be done relatively easily in all three of those scenes - The Procedural can actually be the part that involves an infrastructure heist and investigation, the Social scene can be trading for Aether (Demons can transfer it to each other, you can have caches of Aether that you could make deals for, etc.) and the Combat scene could likely encourage them to harvest Aether from the dross from Angel Numina use.<br /> <br /> And if you don't want to encourage the loophole, there's always the catch-all of it being ridiculously obvious aetheric beacon to the God Machine. It could pretty easily turn into a Combat scene if they try too hard to do that :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}